	// The merge rewrites a file's LOCAL type-name ids into PROJECT-GLOBAL ones in place — the
	// struct/enum LAYOUTS included, which the project registries then hold BY REFERENCE
	// (`commitStructTypes` upserts the artifact's own object, or a settled clone of an inline
	// record's) — so a second fold of the same artifact must not rewrite them again. That is exact
	// rather than defensive: `Queries.resetMergeTargets` does NOT reset `project.typeNames`, so the
	// interner they were folded into is the one still in hand, across the stdlib body-demand
	// fixpoint's re-folds.
